cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "specurve: specification-curve analysis for parameterised estimators"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. When the
  accompanying study is published, cite the paper as well; its reference will be
  added here on acceptance.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Samir
    family-names: Hossain
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8986-0946"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Texas Tech University
    email: samir.hossain@ttu.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/SamirHossain099/specurve"
abstract: >-
  Specification-curve (multiverse) analysis for estimators whose parameters are
  chosen rather than derived, with detrended fluctuation analysis and its
  multifractal extension as the worked case. The grid runner and the curve
  analysis are estimator-agnostic: they take a mapping of analytic choices to
  levels and any callable that turns one specification plus one series into a
  set of estimates, then produce the specification curve, joint inference on
  the median effect across specifications, and one-way and two-way variance
  decompositions identifying which unreported choice moves a result most. Four
  properties are enforced rather than left to the caller: nothing defaults
  silently, failures are recorded rather than dropped, there is exactly one
  definition of the effect size, and a non-finite observed statistic never
  yields a p-value.
keywords:
  - specification curve
  - multiverse analysis
  - detrended fluctuation analysis
  - multifractal analysis
  - heart rate variability
  - analytic flexibility
  - reproducibility
  - reporting standards
license: MIT
